# F-VV-1: does a v_-driven coefficientRestitution reach the contact model mid-run?
# One sphere bounces between two primitive walls (no gravity). e = 0.9 for t < 0.05 s, 0.5 afterwards.
# If the new value propagated, |vz| after each impact past t=0.05 s would be multiplied by ~0.5, not ~0.9.
# NOTE: f_m3 cannot be printed in thermo: FixPropertyGlobal leaves global_freq=0 -> SIGFPE in Thermo::init (legacy).
# Run: mpirun -np 1 lmp -in in.prop_propagation -var every 1
atom_style    granular
atom_modify   map array
boundary      f f f
newton        off
communicate   single vel yes
units         si
region        reg block -0.01 0.01 -0.01 0.01 -0.001 0.021 units box
create_box    1 reg
neighbor      0.0005 bin
neigh_modify  delay 0
variable      e equal "(step*dt < 0.05) * 0.9 + (step*dt >= 0.05) * 0.5"
fix  m1 all property/global youngsModulus peratomtype 1e7
fix  m2 all property/global poissonsRatio peratomtype 0.3
fix  m3 all property/global coefficientRestitution peratomtypepair 1 v_e every ${every}
fix  m4 all property/global coefficientFriction peratomtypepair 1 0.0
pair_style gran model hertz tangential history
pair_coeff * *
timestep 1e-6
fix wz1 all wall/gran model hertz tangential history primitive type 1 zplane 0.0
fix wz2 all wall/gran model hertz tangential history primitive type 1 zplane 0.02
create_atoms 1 single 0.0 0.0 0.01
set atom 1 diameter 0.002 density 2500
velocity all set 0.0 0.0 -1.0
fix integr all nve/sphere
variable vz equal vz[1]
variable z equal z[1]
thermo_style custom step time v_e v_vz v_z
thermo 500
run 150000
